From: tcmay@netcom.com (Timothy C. May)
Subject: Bet 5000...and List Justice (what a combo!)

Mike Price writes:

> I was intending to wait for Tim's "Nazi smear" charge to go through
> adjudication before resuming posting to extropians.  But since I have
> no idea when adjudication will be delivered (it has been nearly 2 weeks
> since I first asked the Adjudicator to consider my case) and Donald is
> champing at the bit (or is that foaming at the mouth) I'll indulge 
> him...  Gee, I never knew I was so popular.

I suspect this whole "list justice" situation is out of hand. I only
filed formal charges to demonstrate that mechanistic application of
rules often results in poor justice, this after I was hit with the
"but rules are rules" justification for the verdict rendered in my
case (wherein Mike Wiik alleged I had insulted and flamed him).

In any case, some of the folks I charged agreed with the gist of the
points, another just shrugged, and a couple got fairly angry. Oh well,
it was "nothing personal." (One of the folks got even angrier when I
told him in e-mail this.)

In Mike's case, we had an exchange of e-mail that I thought was
reasonable and useful. I hope Mike thinks so, too. And I decided to
not post either for an amount equal to the time Harry sentenced him
not to post...a few days, I recall. (Then the list outage hit on top
of that...all in all, a useful break from the List.) As Mike was off
for that entire time, and more, I'd say the whole issue is much more
than moot.

Frankly, with the "::exclude" feature, I don't even see the need for
_any_ list justice system of the sort we have here. Harry's justice
system is indeed quick, these days, but the "rules are rules"
application still seems wrong-headed. And now the delays have shifted
onto the "List Adjudicator," presumably still Andrea Gallagher.

Now Andrea may be a very fine person and all, but she has no visible
presence on the List. That is, where is she? Need I elaborate on this
point?

(If Andrea is in fact reading the list, but for some reason has
decided not to participate, I am sorry for implying she's not in touch
with us. I still favor a "jury" selected somehow from members of the
list...nothing too elaborate, just a small panel, for emergency use only.)

An appeals system that relies on a jurist who has little or no contact
with the parties, who is not an active player--or at least one of the
regular lurkers--and who cannot judge the "tolerance level" of the
list seems like a poor model of a private justice system. Our list has
"community standards" and these should come from the active members of
the list.

If Mike wants to push ahead with the appeal, even though he's been not
posting for far longer than the sentence was, my fear is that whatever
the Adjudicator decides, one way or another, the result will hardly be
definitive and will hardly help resolve these complicated issues of
private justice.

I recommend we drop the formal charges business and instead just
encourage wider use of "::exclude" functions. Save the formal charges
for serious, meta-level issues involving the List as a whole...and at
that level, just kick disrupters off the list "for cause."

Sounds fair enough to me.


--Tim May


